  "sourceNotes": [
    "Calibrated allowances supplied in project narrative; not a manufacturer quote.",
    "CCI values are PLANNING ALLOWANCES, not RSMeans City Cost Index publications. Florida is set to 102 so the 2,000 sf worked example traces. Disclose this in the UI.",
    "Factory-region National / unspecified index is 1.00 so the fixture factory line is 2000 \u00d7 125 = 250000.",
    "terrainCrane (Flat 1.00 / Sloped 1.12 / Difficult 1.25) is a planning fill-in. Do not apply CCI to crane day rates.",
    "fieldFloorFactor (1s 1.00; 2\u20133 1.04; 4\u20135 1.08; 6\u20138 1.14) is a planning fill-in.",
    "Complexity multipliers (Low 0.90 / Med 1.00 / High 1.15 / Very High 1.30) are planning fill-ins and do not apply to transport.",
    "MEP matrix interpolations (documented, not silent): Townhome/Central 36, Townhome/VRF 42; Multifamily/Split 32; Hospitality/Split 44.",
    "standingSeamPremium multiplies the roof line by 1.12 when true.",
    "Factory/field shares per line are explanatory planning fill-ins that sum to 1.00. Volumetric manufacturing is 100% factory; transport/crane/set-stitch are 100% field; roof/siding shares are field-weighted close-up allowances; MEP uses the specified field share (0.25 volumetric / 0.45 panelized).",
    "Fill-ins listed here are planning fill-ins pending qualified modular estimator review.",
    "CCI concept follows an RSMeans-style localization pattern but these figures are not published RSMeans values.",
    "factoryCostReduction 0.80 is applied once after the factory matrix and factors. Do not also bake a 20% cut into factoryPsf.",
    "Live transport is 0.05% of the reduced factory line (factory \u00d7 transportPctOfFactory 0.0005). The historic per-module distance formula is informational only (module count and haul still display).",
    "Product band is \u221210% / +10% (point \u00d7 0.90 / \u00d7 1.10). Actual uncertainty may be wider.",
    "Traditional stick-built comparison (planning allowance): stickPsf is the reduced modular factory+field stack (factory + set/stitch + roof + siding + MEP + sprinkler) \u00d7 stickPremium (~35\u201355% above that stack) plus stickExtrasPsf site-built extras, then the same user contingency. Transport and crane stay on the modular side only. stick.point is never added into includedTotal. If a scenario would violate stick.point > modular.point, clamp stick.point to modular.point \u00d7 stickClampRatio (1.08) and recompute the \u00b110% band so the invariant always holds.",
    "Stick-built schedule is a longer sequential on-site span than the modular on-site window. Modular factory weeks can overlap site/foundation work; foundations remain excluded from cost."
  ],
